{"kind":"request","text":"Uniqueness guards by index, not by scan. Child of the load findings a6847815 (item 1).\n\nFound: from about 1,000 members `add-member` answers 503 `guard-incomplete` (7,818 refusals in the sustained run). HANDLE_UNUSED (packages/platform/src/membership.ts:198) is a `none` range guard with one `equals` of the slot `handle` against the field; `range` (packages/derive/src/guards.ts:88-108) scans at most guardScan (1,000, packages/contract/src/bounds.ts:104) items and answers guard-incomplete when the scan is not complete.\n\nDesign (decided): the derived view keeps an equality index over every slot declared `fixed: true` of each item type, maintained as items are applied. A range guard whose `where` is exactly one `equals` between a fixed slot of the subject type and a field (or a constant) is answered from the index: exact count over the named states, complete, no scan, no guardScan charge. Every other `where` keeps the scan and its guardScan bound. The index is general (any fixed slot), not a handle special case, and it is part of the view the `dap check` replay rebuilds. Document the rule in the contract's guard section and the derive package.\n\nWitness: a room with 2,000 members admits add-member with a new handle and refuses `handle-in-use` for a held one, with no guard-incomplete; `dap check` replays it; a paired control shows a `where` on a non-fixed slot still answering guard-incomplete past guardScan; the existing guard tests unchanged.\n\nOne gate, exact-head review, PD-2 note. Order: after the CLI slice.","body":{"conditions":"The fixed-slot index and the guard rule as stated, documented in the contract and derive package; the witnesses listed; one gate; exact-head checker approval; landed on main.","target_head":"ca7b16bc9a297912a065ca97773b510f6f14dcdc","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}